  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• Boil the kettle. Fill a large saucepan with boiling water over high heat with a pinch of salt.\n• Add spaghetti to the boiling water and cook, over a high heat, until ‘al dente’, 10 minutes.\n• Reserve pasta water (1/3 cup for 2 people / 2/3 cup for 4 people). Drain spaghetti.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-67b34a80062b385ef87c07e4-f8e38254.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Meanwhile, halve snacking tomatoes. Roughly chop kalamata olives and capers.\n• Heat a large frying pan over medium-high heat with a drizzle of olive oil.\n• Cook snacking tomatoes, stirring occasionally, until blistered, 4-5 minutes.\n• Add garlic paste and a pinch of chilli flakes (if using). Cook until fragrant, 1-2 minutes.\n• Add tomato sugo, capers, olives and the reserved pasta water. Simmer until slightly thickened, 1-2 minutes.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-67b34a80062b385ef87c07e4-4e5f0407.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Remove from heat then stir in baby spinach leaves and cooked spaghetti, until wilted, 1-2 minutes. Season to taste.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-67b34a80062b385ef87c07e4-1216a52b.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Divide spaghetti puttanesca between bowls.\n• Top with Parmesan cheese. Tear over parsley to garnish. Crumble over marinated goat cheese to serve. Enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-67b34a80062b385ef87c07e4-235c82dc.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
